$Id$
Public domain. Procedures for building TeX Live and Biber on Cygwin.
From Ken Brown, 19oct2026, on the occasion of his retirement.

#+TITLE: Building texlive

* Set up subversion

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
# Get config file.
https://tug.org/texlive/svn/setup.html
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Checkout source tree

Here we use svn's sparse checkout feature:

http://svnbook.red-bean.com/en/1.8/svn.advanced.sparsedirs.html

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive
svn co svn://$USR:$PASS@tug.org/texlive/trunk --depth immediates
svn update --set-depth exclude trunk/TODO
svn update --set-depth empty trunk/Master/bin
svn update --set-depth infinity trunk/Master/bin/i386-cygwin
svn update --set-depth infinity trunk/Master/bin/x86_64-cygwin
svn update --set-depth empty trunk/Master/tlpkg
svn update --set-depth infinity trunk/Master/tlpkg/tlpsrc
svn update --set-depth empty trunk/Master/tlpkg/bin
svn update trunk/Master/tlpkg/bin/tl-update-bindir
svn update --set-depth empty trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer
svn update --set-depth empty trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer/xz
svn update trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer/xz/xz.i386-cygwin.exe
svn update trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer/xz/xz.x86_64-cygwin.exe
svn update --set-depth empty trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer/lz4
svn update trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer/lz4/lz4.i386-cygwin.exe
svn update trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer/lz4/lz4.x86_64-cygwin.exe
svn update --set-depth immediates trunk/Build
svn update --set-depth exclude trunk/Build/logs
svn update --set-depth exclude trunk/Build/tests
svn update --set-depth exclude trunk/Build/README
svn update --set-depth infinity trunk/Build/source
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Update source tree

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive/trunk
svn up
#+END_EXAMPLE
   
* Clean up old build directory

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive/build
old_build_datetime=$(ls -l Work/build.log | gawk '{ print $6 "." $7 }')
cp -p Work/build.log ../${old_build_datetime}-build.log
rm -rf Work inst
#+END_EXAMPLE


* Update build directory

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive/trunk/Build
rsync -av --delete source/ ../../build/
#+END_EXAMPLE

   

* Build

=~/src/clisp-texlive= contains a stripped-down version of =clisp=,
without dynamic modules.  If I build =xindy= with the system =clisp=,
the resulting =xindy-lisp= complains that it can’t find =lisp.exe=.
This must have something to do with the way =clisp= is built to
support dynamic modules.  I build =clisp-texlive= using

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
https://github.com/kbrow1i/clisp-texlive.git
#+END_EXAMPLE

If this is too much trouble, the next maintainer can simply build
without =xindy=.

The CXXFLAGS setting avoids the "too many sections" assembler error when
building harfbuzz.

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive/build
JOBS=$(($(nproc) + 1))
TL_CONFIGURE_ARGS=\
"-C \
--enable-xindy \
--enable-shared \
--enable-silent-rules \
CLISP=/home/kbrown/src/clisp-texlive/clisp-2.49.92-1.x86_64/build/clisp.exe \
CXXFLAGS='-Wa,-mbig-obj -g -O2' \
LDFLAGS='-Wl,--no-insert-timestamp -Wl,--stack,0x800000'" \
TL_MAKE_FLAGS="-j$JOBS --jobserver-style=pipe -k" ./Build
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Building asymptote

From https://www.tug.org/texlive/build.html#asymptote

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
If necessary, download gc-7.6.2 into ~/src/texlive before starting:

  wget https://github.com/ivmai/bdwgc/releases/download/v7.6.2/gc-7.6.2.tar.gz

cd ~/src/texlive/build/utils/asymptote
tar -xf ../../../gc-7.6.2.tar.gz
./configure \
        --prefix=/tmp/asyinst \
        --enable-texlive-build \
	--disable-lsp \
	--disable-curl \
        --disable-fftw \
        --disable-gsl \
&& make GC=gc-7.6.2 && make check && strip asy
cp asy.exe ../../../trunk/Master/bin/x86_64-cygwin/
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Commit binaries

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive/trunk
svn up

Master/tlpkg/bin/tl-update-bindir --bin-loc ~/src/texlive/build/inst/bin/x86_64-pc-cygwin/ x86_64-cygwin
svn commit -m "Update 2026 binaries for x86_64-cygwin"
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Building xz

From https://www.tug.org/texlive/build.html#xz

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive
VERSION=5.6.0
wget https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz/releases/download/v${VERSION}/xz-${VERSION}.tar.xz

[Or download from trunk/Master/source]

tar -xf xz-${VERSION}.tar.xz

rsync -av --delete xz-${VERSION}/ build-xz/

cd build-xz
./configure --disable-nls --disable-shared --disable-threads && make
strip src/xz/xz.exe
cp src/xz/xz.exe ../trunk/Master/tlpkg/installer/xz/xz.x86_64-cygwin.exe
#+END_EXAMPLE


#+TITLE: Building biber

* Set up git repos

This has changed since I got commit rights.

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive
git clone git@github.com:plk/biber.git
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Clean up old build directory

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
./Build realclean   # Have to run as admin.
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Update source tree

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive/biber
git pull
cd ..
rsync -av --delete --exclude=.git --exclude=scancache biber/ biber64/
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Build

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
cd ~/src/texlive/biber64
perl Build.PL
./Build test
./Build install # (run as admin; maybe capture output for later
                # uninstall; or could later run ./Build fakeinstall, or
                # look at .../.packlist?
cd dist/cygwin64
./build.sh # might need to first update absolute paths in biber.files and build.sh
#+END_EXAMPLE

Note: If I had to change =biber.files= or =biber.sh=, I need to commit
the changes to Phil Kime’s github repo.

* Commit binaries to SourceForge

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
mv biber-cygwin64.exe biber.exe
tar -cvzf biber-cygwin64.tar.gz biber.exe
scp biber-cygwin64.tar.gz $USR,biblatex-biber@frs.sourceforge.net:/home/frs/project/biblatex-biber/biblatex-biber/current/binaries/Cygwin/
#+END_EXAMPLE

* Upload biber-cygwin package to CTAN

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
VERSION=2.22 # [or 2.22-1,...]
mkdir -p ~/src/texlive/ctan/biblio/biber
cd ~/src/texlive/ctan/biblio/biber
rm biber-cygwin/*.tar.gz
cp ~/src/texlive/biber64/dist/cygwin64/biber-cygwin64.tar.gz biber-cygwin/biber-${VERSION}-cygwin_x86_64.tar.gz
tar -cvzf biber-cygwin.tar.gz biber-cygwin/*
#+END_EXAMPLE

Now go to https://ctan.org/upload and upload =biber-cygwin.tar.gz=,
using =VERSION= as the version and =biblio/biber/biber-cygwin= as the
suggested CTAN directory.

* Uninstall local Biber

#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
rm /usr/local/share/man/man1/biber.1
rm -rf /usr/local/share/perl5/site_perl/5.32/Biber*
rm /usr/local/share/man/man3/Biber*.3pm
rm /usr/local/bin/biber
#+END_EXAMPLE

